{
 "source": "unlockdb.xml.orig",
 "how": "MCC names every customization item it gates in Data/UI/unlockdb.xml (eUnlockItemId_CUSTOMIZATION_<game>_<slot>_<name>). This matches those names against the list of each game's original content (maps/_looks/original_content.json, docs/research/13) and writes maps/_looks/mcc_items.json: for each game, the MCC ids that are original (with the list's item name) and the ones that are MCC additions. What MCC's list holds differs by game (Oct 24): - Reach: every original item AND the additions (MCC gates all Reach armor behind its season pass) - Halo 3, Halo 2 Anniversary, CE, Halo 2: additions only (their original items are always unlocked, so not listed) - Halo 4: the original DLC sets (Mark V, ODST, Ricochet) plus additions; its armor effects are all additions - ODST: each character as separate helmet-on / helmet-off items (one original character each), plus additions An MCC item the list does not name counts as an addition; open cases are printed.",
